From bef369aaaf87d1fcd1cb568d2e5284da65abbc57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@ubuntu.localdomain>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:41:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] feat(rlharness): lethal geometry, events, shadow null
 device and fork helpers

Tracked source changes that the v4.0.0 builds rl_pbo, rl_hazard, rl_hazard2,
rl_laser, rl_score and rl_events were compiled from:

- HAZARDS / PLAYER / BULLETS / ENEMIES / LASERS / ITEMS: per-frame lethal
  geometry export (EXP-P1-001, EXP-P1-004, EXP-P1-005, EXP-P1-021).
- EVENTS: death, bomb, game_over and stage_clear event bits (EXP-P1-005,
  EXP-P2-004, EXP-P2-009).
- Laser damageable-window fields and score fields appended to the existing
  rows; the 25-field HASH prefix is unchanged (EXP-P1-021, G2 report).
- CHILD handles plus fork/park/spawn helpers restricted to a null-device,
  single-threaded shadow (EXP-P0-050, EXP-P1-007), with a startup preflight
  that refuses any other configuration.
- Constant FPS HUD text while the harness is active, so rendered pixels stay
  deterministic (EXP-P0-056).
- Pure replay recorder path and the TH08_ASYNC_READBACK readback path
  (EXP-P0-051, EXP-P0-061, EXP-P0-067).

Binary identities of the builds made from these sources are recorded in
Document/Update/Alpha/v4.0.0/builds.md.
